    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Close out messaging-communication-app-r2 (Communication Workspace) from the MAIN SESSION only:

    1. **README → Complete + graduation criteria** — flip the project README status to Complete; summarize what shipped (W0–W8: two schema deltas + participant junction + ADR, the `by-regarding` + filtered `query` read endpoints, the regarding-mode Timeline on all 11 forms + summary card, the rich `communications-list` widget upgrade, the standalone All-Communications page, the participant index + `participant=` facet, compose-form enrichment, the 3-tier auto-threading policy + thread naming re-derive + RegardingResolver placement, seam tests, docs) and **annotate each of the 9 spec Success Criteria** as met (or documented as owner-handoff/deferred).

    2. **Lessons-learned** — author `notes/lessons-learned.md` capturing: the two shared-`Services/Communication/`-path edits (050 participant write + 070 auto-threading) + their characterization-guard outcomes; the ADR-034 path-C two-typed-lookups decision (participant junction); the ADR-046 path-C RegardingResolver-on-thread-form reuse; the T-1 VisualHost count-only boundary; the impersonation + 2-rule read model (no membership-union) and the access-parity negatives; the dual-deploy discipline (LegalWorkspace + SpaarkeAi widget); publish-size trajectory vs the ~46.99 MB baseline; the notification-spine reserve-only alignment (NFR-06) for a future poll→push increment; and deferred items (category/tags, thread-grain participant rows, permanent sitemap entry, poll→push).

    3. **`/test-diet` gate (MANDATORY, root §7)** — invoke `/test-diet` to reconcile every test added/modified during R2 (esp. task 080's vertical-slice seam + access-parity + characterization tests) against the ADR-038 build-vs-maintain classifier: MAINTAIN-class tests stay at KEEP paths; SCAFFOLDING-class tests are emitted for deletion (`git rm`); AMBIGUOUS require reviewer judgment. The skill is read-only — it emits commands for the reviewer. Output: `notes/test-diet-report.md`. The wrap-up PR MUST cite this report.

    4. **Final `code-review`** — run a final holistic `code-review` across the R2 close-out diff surface as a project-close quality gate (special attention: the security-sensitive access-parity/read model [no membership-union] + the two shared-path edits 050/070).

    5. **`/devops-project-archive`** — archive the project (set Status + Closed Date, capture counts, close the Issue, retain the folder + `.archived` marker; worktree preserved per operator workflow).

    6. **Final TASK-INDEX reconciliation** — confirm every W0–W8 task is ✅ (or explicitly documented as deferred/owner-handoff, e.g. any PCF/form import or schema deploy handed to the owner); set `current-task.md` to "none — project complete".

    Then confirm the project is complete and ready for `merge-to-master`.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke project lead running the main-session project-close protocol. Authoritative on the wrap-up sequence, the `/test-diet` gate (root §7), the final `code-review` gate, and `/devops-project-archive`. Does NOT delegate to subagents (root §3 write boundary).
  </role>

  <goal>
    README status is Complete with the 9 Success Criteria annotated; `notes/lessons-learned.md` and `notes/test-diet-report.md` exist; the `/test-diet` gate has run and its report is cited; a final `code-review` has run with Critical findings addressed; the project is archived via `/devops-project-archive`; TASK-INDEX is fully reconciled; `current-task.md` is "none — project complete". The project is ready to merge to master.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      This is the project-close task. Per root §7, a `090-wrapup-*` task invokes `/test-diet` BEFORE marking the project complete — reconciling R2's test additions against the ADR-038 KEEP-path categories (task 080's seam + access-parity + characterization tests are the bulk). R2 was substantial (two schema deltas + a participant junction, new read/query endpoints on the impersonation path, a 3-tier auto-threading policy on the shared resolver, a participant-index write on the shared persist path, Surface 1 on all 11 forms, a rich widget upgrade with dual-deploy, and a standalone page). The notification-spine reserve-only alignment (NFR-06) is forward-facing — record it for the future poll→push increment.
    </background>
